.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH soundcraft-cli-mcp 1  "mcp " 
.SH NAME
soundcraft\-cli\-mcp \- Serve MCP on stdin and stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsoundcraft\-cli mcp\fR [\fB\-\-connect\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-automation\-read\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-automation\-write\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve MCP on stdin and stdout
.PP
The automation roots confine every file the agent\*(Aqs commands read (open, import, presets) and write (save, bounce, export) to those folders, links followed. Each root flag may be given more than once, a path inside any of its folders being allowed, and a kind left out grants none of its access. The roots confine the in\-process server, so they, like \-\-demo, conflict with \-\-connect.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Serve a running app\*(Aqs control channel at this port or host:port instead of an in\-process engine; conflicts with \-\-demo, which starts only that engine
.TP
\fB\-\-demo\fR
Start the in\-process engine from the demo session
.TP
\fB\-\-automation\-read\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
A folder the agent\*(Aqs commands may read from; repeat for several
.TP
\fB\-\-automation\-write\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
A folder the agent\*(Aqs commands may write to; repeat for several
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
